<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:56:32Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Zelensky holds US talks as Trump accuses him of not wanting peace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b003d24dbf3effdb4bd86387b9e64a18570ac52145a9a47a006f9b1488f37e5</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:56:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T21:59:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-zelensky-war-trump-peace-russia-sanctions--71a514130b55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-zelensky-war-trump-peace-russia-sanctions" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky spoke with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner on Sunday amid tensions after President Donald Trump accused Kyiv of resisting peace with Russia. The talks came as both sides exchanged attacks on energy infrastructure, while Washington’s easing of Russian sanctions raised concerns among European allies.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian drone attack on Saint Petersburg kills one, sets refinery ablaze</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01b6f1ab86c7c20939489efcb3cac888d604a47e0086fc88f166cd8e5127bb97</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T12:03:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-sets-saint-petersburg-refinery-ablaze-in-large-scale-drone-attack--5c56492efee9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-sets-saint-petersburg-refinery-ablaze-in-large-scale-drone-attack" /><summary type="html">A large-scale Ukrainian drone attack on Russia's second-largest city Saint Petersburg killed at least one person and hospitalised another five on Sunday. The attack – which also sparked fires at an oil refinery and depot – comes as Kyiv accused Russia of violating Washington's "energy ceasefire" dozens of times.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Macron denounces 'unbridled' violence as France hit by new clashes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4750e97e17ca935e9a40e07fea437e5149b7534cfa5e371dee4ed1d8a098f558</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T03:09:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france--a2aec9eab7bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france" /><summary type="html">President Emmanuel Macron on Sunday slammed the "unbridled" violence that erupted in cost-of-living protests across France, as police battled protesters and looters in new clashes in Paris. Nearly 2,400 people were arrested and at least 1,000 police and gendarmes injured, the interior ministry said. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo returns to Vatican four days after lung cancer surgery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bd189663630b7c157ab218b14c42708fd432f9d89e78b943d592002b5b5bd73</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:35:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261017-pope-leo-returns-to-vatican-four-days-after-lung-cancer-surgery--7b385513b4cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261017-pope-leo-returns-to-vatican-four-days-after-lung-cancer-surgery" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV was released from the hospital on Saturday after lung cancer surgery. Doctors removed part of the 71-year-old's right lung last week to extract a cancerous tumour.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky fears Trump 'will continue' to lift Russia sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8694b5875e67d9da4adf9c17c9be18e3720d450e5e070e57e73028ead9f83bdc</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T20:25:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-zelensky-turns-to-europe-for-backing-as-ties-with-trump-deteriorate--5f558b124f49.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-zelensky-turns-to-europe-for-backing-as-ties-with-trump-deteriorate" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said on Saturday that he feared his US counterpart Donald Trump "will continue" lifitng sanctions on Russia. Zelensky's relationship with Trump deteriorated after the Washington eased sanctions on Moscow as part of a diesel-supply deal, despite Russia increasing strikes on Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Finish what we started': After student protests, France braces for return of the Yellow Vests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:690183f76435d7913665015c350f16ad34bebdd2a91b50c251b4a5db6defe838</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T20:10:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-finish-what-we-started-after-student-protests-france-braces-return-yellow-vests--89fbb6304652.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-finish-what-we-started-after-student-protests-france-braces-return-yellow-vests" /><summary type="html">An online movement against rising fuel prices has gained momentum ahead of planned nationwide demonstrations on October 17 with former Yellow Vest figures set to join the protests in support of high-school students. Some are drawing parallels between the latest action and the 2018 cost-of-living protests that rattled President Emmanuel Macron's first term in office.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Clashes grip Tirana as Albanian PM blames 'foreign hands' for mounting unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d72a98d1d30dc8881c8abd726363845a430df6f56d8d93254621e3d3393cd784</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:59:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-clashes-grip-tirana-as-albanian-pm-blames-foreign-hands--fa019f033795.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-clashes-grip-tirana-as-albanian-pm-blames-foreign-hands" /><summary type="html">Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama on Friday blamed the involvement of “foreign hands” for escalating protests, which he said are aimed at hindering Albania's bid to join the European Union. Thousands of demonstrators have taken to the streets of Albania's capital since Tuesday, demanding Rama’s resignation and denouncing university conditions and high tuition fees.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump Vs Zelensky, From the Screen to the Streets, Gen Z protests from Paris to Dehli</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b377d4063ccbf1a60014403639dea637f7062f6e74ef862277fbd3964c6353f</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:21:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261016-trump-vs-zelensky-from-the-screen-to-the-streets-gen-z-protests-from-paris-to-dehli--b61c04ba3eb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261016-trump-vs-zelensky-from-the-screen-to-the-streets-gen-z-protests-from-paris-to-dehli" /><summary type="html">In India, the Cockroach movement felt the crushing boot of the state this week. Thousands of Gen Z protesters were rounded up and detained in sports stadiums and community halls turned into makeshift detention centres, while the movement’s founder, Abhijeet Dipke, was arrested on arrival. A mass demonstration over alleged voter fraud was effectively crushed before it could begin.And Abdijeet has been detained again todayNarendra Modi’s government says the measures were necessary to protect civilians in the capital. But he now faces accusations of choosing repression over democracy, with the UN Human Rights Office urging authorities to respect the right to peaceful assembly. 
 
 
 
It’s been a week of blame games and accusations of betrayal in Ukraine with President Zelensky speaking of his personal hurt at President Trump’s decision to make a diesel deal with the Kremlin ahead of the US Mid term elections calling it “weak”, suggesting Trump had chosen, “the other side”. Trump meanwhile made clear he wants Zelensky replaced, and warned him against striking Russian refineries AND announced an energy ceasefire, declaring it to have been agreed by both sides but which went nowhere. President Zelensky continued to search for solidarity and a solution in Europe.
 
 
 
It’s been a week of blame games and accusations of betrayal in Ukraine with President Zelensky speaking of his personal hurt at President Trump’s decision to make a diesel deal with the Kremlin ahead of the US Mid term elections calling it “weak”, suggesting Trump had chosen, “the other side”. Trump meanwhile made clear he wants Zelensky replaced, and warned him against striking Russian refineries AND announced an energy ceasefire, declaring it to have been agreed by both sides but which went nowhere. President Zelensky continued to search for solidarity and a solution in Europe. 
 
 
 
Gavin Lee is joined this week by Anne-Elisabeth Moutet, John Sweeney, Victor Mallet and Suhasini Raj.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>'US tilting toward Russia: Europeans are standing more and more solidly with Zelensky'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cce52eb8e6f95e1897d93c08e3888c528cc7e6615473f4d7c466d3828715cbca</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T18:33:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261016-us-tilting-toward-russia-europeans-are-standing-more-and-more-solidly-with-zelensky--9c931bc73795.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261016-us-tilting-toward-russia-europeans-are-standing-more-and-more-solidly-with-zelensky" /><summary type="html">As transatlantic relations confront renewed geopolitical uncertainty, former Estonian President Toomas Hendrik Ilves delivers a pointed assessment of Washington's shifting approach to Russia's war on Ukraine and the profound implications for European security. At the heart of his analysis lies a fundamental question: can Europe develop the political unity, strategic independence and military capabilities necessary to defend its interests in an increasingly unpredictable international order?  Ilves response: "If there's any time for Europe to begin to act as Europe and not as being strictly self-interested, then this is the time for it."</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>The risks faced by women migrants in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6946104f19586b67a7712fb9bd53f1b56a9f0c2a9785bbde8c2f7fd05e162436</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:05:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261016-the-risks-faced-by-women-migrants-in-europe--cd5d50e9d3bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261016-the-risks-faced-by-women-migrants-in-europe" /><summary type="html">This October marks 10 years since French police dismantled the notorious Calais "Jungle" camp. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin returns to the region to explore what has changed for migrants over the past decade. She joins Annette Young and Dr Marissa Quie of Cambridge University to discuss migration routes and their growing role in European political debate.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV celebrates mass in hospital while recovering from lung cancer operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c22d784163d89d11174f46bc8a1c9df1fafffac48db910bd74dc2abe0735f68c</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:57:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-in-hospital-while-recovering-from-lung-cancer-operation--19afdf0fb464.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-in-hospital-while-recovering-from-lung-cancer-operation" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV celebrated a mass at Rome's Gemelli hospital Friday after undergoing surgery to remove a cancerous tumour from his right lung, photos released by the Vatican showed. Doctors said his recovery was progressing normally but that further tests would show whether the cancer had spread.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'America, with this president, is not our ally. Trump is a liar': French MEP Bernard Guetta</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e03bea24a26c260a07162e21ede534648b9615adae4fe81359cad903546e36bb</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:55:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261016-america-with-this-president-is-not-our-ally-trump-is-a-liar-french-mep-bernard-guetta--b1bd5be51426.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261016-america-with-this-president-is-not-our-ally-trump-is-a-liar-french-mep-bernard-guetta" /><summary type="html">Our guest is veteran French journalist and commentator Bernard Guetta, who is a Member of the European Parliament for the centrist Renew group. He tells the programme that Donald Trump is "a liar, because he tried to tell the American people that Zelensky and the Ukrainian resistance were responsible for the price of diesel. This is a pure lie. He (Trump) is responsible because he started the war with Iran." Guetta goes on to say that "without American intelligence sharing, Ukraine is weaker and weaker. That's terrible, to see the president of the United States giving a hand to Putin against Ukraine."</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU and Canada seek closer ties: Will Canada become the EU's first associate member?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82cb535a3a9d64d049aea1c713b40f8ce523043f6803d2e0ff6dd1a3f280b4be</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:04:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261016-eu-and-canada-seek-closer-ties-will-canada-become-the-eu-s-first-associate-member--ed7e333e056c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261016-eu-and-canada-seek-closer-ties-will-canada-become-the-eu-s-first-associate-member" /><summary type="html">As the international context becomes more challenging for the European Union, the bloc is looking to boost its ties with like-minded allies. Canada is part of that architecture that the EU says it wants to build. The big news of EU Commission President Ursula von der Leyen's State of the Union speech in September was that Canada could become an associate member – an arrangement that does not exist for the EU's partners at the moment.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UK bookstores scramble as Sally Rooney's novels pulled over Palestine Action support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d3bbf33a7927eeb95bd30c8546ae74c8364d96b40c857822811d2750a01398f</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T06:15:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-uk-bookstores-scramble-as-sally-rooney-novels-pulled-over-palestine-action-support--9a377dc7e2dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-uk-bookstores-scramble-as-sally-rooney-novels-pulled-over-palestine-action-support" /><summary type="html">Critically acclaimed Irish novelist Sally Rooney's announcement that her books could no longer be sold in the UK due to her support for proscribed group Palestine Action has left British booksellers rushing to stock up on her works before distributors run out. The British government's ban on the group, which practiced non-violent direct action and sabotage against UK military assets believed to be working with the Israeli government, makes support for Palestine Action punishable by up to 14 years in prison.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's backers will 'be looking at' Kyiv's €70 billion request, Macron says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4acb12a353a3d1b981cc65c89764f3b6558f83b8c9f3264c44cd5499b35e0051</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T01:50:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace--6cfecd7f8863.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said the EU will “not abandon Ukraine and the Ukrainian people” and that Kyiv’s request for extra funds will be examined, while addressing the media at a summit in Brussels Friday. Earlier, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky asked EU leaders to provide Kyiv with an extra €70 billion next year to help with the country's ongoing fight against Russia. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Minibus crashes into train at French Channel Tunnel entrance, injuring 19</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80943c657620eb4a7209f93bf332cff23af6b4c36026978fa1a1376d83296e35</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T00:53:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-19-injured-as-minibus-crashes-into-train-at-channel-tunnel-entrance--79f37e5f8958.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-19-injured-as-minibus-crashes-into-train-at-channel-tunnel-entrance" /><summary type="html">Nineteen people were injured Thursday when a minibus carrying truck drivers crashed into a vehicle shuttle train at the French entrance to the Channel Tunnel near Calais, forcing a 90-minute suspension of shuttle services. Two people were hospitalised with serious but non-life-threatening injuries, French authorities said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France and Germany agree to ease EU car emissions rules in new deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9932e54e1b7238077216ec1fec20f02e18d5e11d6d3b31a913e5fb5c551533d</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T23:48:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-and-germany-agree-to-ease-eu-car-emissions-rules-in-new-deal--9bcf5af8133a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-and-germany-agree-to-ease-eu-car-emissions-rules-in-new-deal" /><summary type="html">Paris and Berlin on Friday confirmed their deal aimed at protecting Europe's struggling automotive sector, having reached agreements on the flashpoint issues of EU car emissions and "made in Europe" components. A draft deal reviewed Thursday showed the two countries backing looser EU emissions rules for carmakers.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky rallies European allies as US support for Ukraine wanes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecad6a43474593118a4a7fee40ec923122b35d863ad740564a13b5a400b9d030</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T23:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-us-support-for-ukraine-wanes--820569914737.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-us-support-for-ukraine-wanes" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky sought European backing Thursday after vowing to resume strikes on Russian oil refineries despite US President Donald Trump’s demands to stop. Tensions between Kyiv and Washington have escalated in recent days over sanctions, energy infrastructure attacks and restrictions on satellite communications.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Sally Rooney's books cannot be sold in UK amid Palestine Action ban, publisher says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2fa84c8ae1e23cfef6baab1bb481165a735b550cdb629f4c58ab27838bf5f0a</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T21:15:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261015-sally-rooney-books-cannot-be-sold-in-uk-amid-palestine-action-ban-publisher--6528f0929ba4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261015-sally-rooney-books-cannot-be-sold-in-uk-amid-palestine-action-ban-publisher" /><summary type="html">Irish author Sally Rooney can no longer sell her books in the UK because of her support for the activist group Palestine Action, her publisher Faber said on Wednesday. Rooney has previously expressed her support for the group, which was banned as a "terrorist" organisation by the UK government in July 2025. It is not banned in Ireland, where Rooney lives. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alan Greene, Professor of Constitutional Law and Human Rights at the Birmingham Law School.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>'It is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties', Romanian MEP</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8bbadd68c71d5bfae76df6e0b84b3c9007f742926a63476d5d98a14f2747899</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T20:03:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/it-is-clear-that-sooner-or-later-we-will-have-european-casualties-romanian-mep--8a7157699d26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/it-is-clear-that-sooner-or-later-we-will-have-european-casualties-romanian-mep" /><summary type="html">Rescuers searched on Thursday for seven missing sailors after drones struck two chemical tankers near Romania's Black Sea coast, setting them ablaze and raising fresh security concerns along a vital shipping route used by Ukraine. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Europe editor Armen Georgian, Nicolae Stefanuta, Romanian MEP and Co-Chair of the Group of the Greens, says that the Danube delta region is facing a more intense threat from Russia than Baltic States and that "it is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties".</summary></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump 'openly financing Russia's war with Ukraine', Nobel peace laureate says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:613f6ff835a8d483ed9b70ddfb5218d28ce8984231d90047e15fc3d5f8a1ab16</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:48:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-openly-financing-russia-s-war-with-ukraine-nobel-peace-laureate-says--5033be605410.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-openly-financing-russia-s-war-with-ukraine-nobel-peace-laureate-says" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Nobel Peace laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that with the diesel-supply deal with Moscow Donald Trump "is openly financing this war, by lifting sanctions is providing Russia with opportunities to earn more money" adding that "extra money will be converted in rockets and drones and additional deaths among the civilian population".</summary></entry><entry><title>Seven missing off Romania after latest Black Sea drone attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1237d2218f9f968c4e6197b8e2eb5258f8940fe0e955e5b2f3a4683cbe0a671c</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:04:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks--33513f001314.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks" /><summary type="html">Romania reported seven people missing on Thursday after two drone attacks on ships in the Black Sea, where several vessels have been hit recently in suspected fallout from the Ukraine war. The attacks are the latest in a series off the coast of Romania and neighbouring Bulgaria in recent weeks. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Albania's leader defies calls to resign as student protesters rampage in capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd8f4a896d80ec6704a111b2aa2a0c1d1beb088f668ae5b5796f5627d4db7b98</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T19:02:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/albania-s-leader-defies-calls-to-resign-as-student-protesters-rampage-in-capital--247a1ee2a654.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/albania-s-leader-defies-calls-to-resign-as-student-protesters-rampage-in-capital" /><summary type="html">​Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama on Thursday rejected calls to resign as thousands of student-led protesters smashed windows and fought running battles with riot police firing water cannon and tear gas in the capital. The demonstrators accuse officials of corruption and neglecting education and say they are angry about the sale of parts of Albania's southern coastline to a luxury resort development backed ​by US President ‌Donald Trump's son-in-law Jared Kushner. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Trump really pull the plug? Starlink restored but Ukraine's fate still uncertain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76d2c762c66c9998eadc61a5d30bb3f38298057047c0209fec9627aebc0c3863</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T18:38:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261015-will-trump-really-pull-the-plug-starlink-restored-but-ukraine-s-fate-still-uncertain--2088cc5dba32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261015-will-trump-really-pull-the-plug-starlink-restored-but-ukraine-s-fate-still-uncertain" /><summary type="html">Can a flick of a switch really be enough for Donald Trump and Elon Musk to end Ukraine's hopes of holding out against Russia? With Kyiv already reeling from daily strikes by Russia's new motor-powered drones, the US decision to slow SpaceX's Starlink service was felt immediately on Wednesday, when air raid warnings failed.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Why have US-Ukraine relations soured ahead of the midterms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3facbc66c6079a76d9b3b92f81b8a84f65a4fa12810a95e5339c6e539661cc11</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T17:54:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-why-have-us-ukraine-relations-soured-ahead-of-the-midterms--b38db7502a5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-why-have-us-ukraine-relations-soured-ahead-of-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said he felt “betrayed” on Wednesday after access was seemingly restricted to US intelligence and Space X satellite services, raising new questions about US commitment to Ukraine. With Trump under pressure over rising fuel prices, is the White House hoping criticism of Kyiv can help shift the blame?</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'We're done': Ukraine resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries as 'only leverage' for peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37bb3009e41f49dbe2c9ce52dd3ce476adc05df9dbff3490e5b0fff935e113a0</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T16:14:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-tal--b4d9641c071b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261015-we-re-done-ukraine-resumes-strikes-on-russian-oil-refineries-as-only-leverage-for-peace-talks-1" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. As Zelensky declares Ukraine "done" with Trump's self-declared energy ceasefire and resumes strikes on Russian oil refineries, Zalmayev warns: "When you talk about the energy ceasefire, it presupposes two to be able to tango and to dance this dance." He challenges the legitimacy of Trump's unilateral announcement, made without agreement between Moscow and Kyiv, as Russia continues attacking Ukraine's energy infrastructure. Yet he cautions that Zelensky may need tactical restraint to preserve vital US support. Zalmayev also examines Western sanctions, frozen Russian assets, and Washington's pursuit of economic normalization with Moscow without meaningful Russian concessions.</summary></entry><entry><title>NATO to address drone attacks in the Black Sea after seven missing off Romania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2e0e264a1b3a8e54b1a070215e9c1176aea6d49a73220b00ac980a88e38710a</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:35:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks--d31e01c8ba8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks" /><summary type="html">NATO will put drone strikes in the Black Sea on its agenda at a meeting next week, officials said Thursday, following two new attacks and the disappearance of seven people. Incidents involving civilian vessels in the Black Sea have been on the rise off the coasts of Bulgaria and Romania in a suspected spillover from Russia’s war in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Student protests spread in Albania as demonstrators call for PM resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8be2a760b78a04b809289c875b23186d69d2ea149a0a7109aae4108825b5a76</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T12:27:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-student-protests-escalate-in-albania-as-demonstrators-call-for-pm-resignation--ceb6c228c280.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-student-protests-escalate-in-albania-as-demonstrators-call-for-pm-resignation" /><summary type="html">Clashes broke out between demonstrators and police for the third consecutive day on Thursday in Albania, with Prime Minister Edi Rama condemning the “chaos” that caused damage to government buildings. Thousands of protesters are calling for Rama's resignation and better studying conditions for Albanian students.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia detains independent outlet Novaya Gazeta editor Sergei Sokolov</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f072f90ce6532850dd343f6282fa1dfbb3bb6f184f93d21423bd8711a0f5730e</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T11:39:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-russia-detains-novaya-gazeta-editor-in-chief-sergei-sokolov-after-home-search--614591d58672.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-russia-detains-novaya-gazeta-editor-in-chief-sergei-sokolov-after-home-search" /><summary type="html">Sergei Sokolov, the editor-in-chief of Russia's independent newspaper Novaya Gazeta, was detained and taken for questioning on Thursday after authorities searched his home, the newspaper said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'American abandonment' threatens Ukraine's civilians in war against Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f38540e52dbc32034f9e48e7597272cb401184790ba0d66d2238acb16cad7200</id><updated>2026-10-19T04:55:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T11:09:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261015-american-abandonment-threatens-ukraine-s-civilians-in-war-against-russia--f328a2383f92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261015-american-abandonment-threatens-ukraine-s-civilians-in-war-against-russia" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 15: First, reported Starlink disruptions in Ukraine make the European front pages. Next, US papers go into more detail about the situation. Also, an unusual alliance forms in Germany between far-right and far-left parties. Meanwhile, the winners of the Wildlife Photographer of the Year awards have been announced. Finally, Finland flaunts its smelly islands.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry></feed>
